welcome back for another edition of  modeling the Masters where we look at  the successful strategies of famous  entrepreneurs my name is Evan Carmichael  and I wanted to start off by thanking  everybody who watched the last episode  on Harley Davidson we've received almost  3,000 viewers so far and I wanted to  continue the tradition today by talking  about another successful entrepreneur  Milton Hershey now while you may know  Hershey foods today for its five billion  dollars in revenue eleven thousand  employees and all of his chocolate bars  when the company was first started it  was started by a young entrepreneur  Milton Hershey who was eighteen years  old had no money to his name and had to  borrow $100 to his aunt just to get the  company off the ground so today we're  going to learn about three factors that  led to his success lesson number one is  be persistent when Milton Hershey first  got started he moved to Philadelphia  started a new candy store and he worked  15 16 hour days every day to get the  business off the ground he would make  his candy overnight and then during the  day go out and sell it after six years  of trying and trying and trying the  company eventually failed to thought I'm  going to keep going I'm going to try it  again in with the Chicago started the  same business that I also failed you  didn't give up move to New Orleans  try it again failed again closed down  the business start it up again in New  York tried to get the business off the  ground we're starting to get a few sales  coming in but then he had his entire  shop and inventory wrapped by a group of  three children so we had to again  declare bankruptcy shut down the  business and after ten years of trying  and trying and trying he didn't give up  he started new businesses again and  eventually was able to build this  successful company that we know today  most entrepreneurs give up way too  easily I'm not suggesting spend 10 years  of failure to try to get your business  off the ground but don't quit at the  first sign of trouble you may have to  try something new you may have to move  to new market bring new features in sell  to new customers don't give up the first  sign of failure most entrepreneurs fail  not because they have a  idea just because they give up too  quickly lesson number two is innovate  after trying the same thing over and  over and over again in four different  cities after 10 years her she decided I  gotta try something different so the big  innovation that he did was he moved from  caramels to chocolate in 1893 there was  a new machine that was on the market in  Europe that could help mass-produced  chocolate so he decided the future was  in chocolate he was going to do  something different he was going to  stand out from everybody else and he was  going to be the first guy to make  chocolate through machine up until that  point  chocolate was available but was handmade  and for people with a lot of money it  was a luxury item and by using the  machine he was able to mass-produce  chocolate similar to what Henry Ford did  for the automobile first she was able to  do for the chocolate industry so finally  he realized I got to do something  different I got to get out there I gotta  innovate and he was the first one to  bring mass-produced chocolate to the  North American market which is one of  the main reasons why he was able to  achieve such success so look at your own  business are you doing something  different are you standing out from the  market are you being innovative do  something that is unique that nobody  else has because if you're doing the  same thing that everybody else is doing  in selling the same product same service  in the same way then you could spend 10  years of your life like Milton Hershey  did trying and trying and trying and not  getting anywhere it's not until you  stand out and do something different  that you're really going to be able to  take your company to that next level of  success lesson number three is treat  people with respect when Milton Hershey  after ten years of failure came back  home his parents actually disowned them  they didn't want anything to do with  them they thought he was a failure he  spent ten years and all this money  basically wasting his time in their  opinion so yet nowhere to go the only  person he was able to call on was  actually one of his former employees  Henry who gave him room and board who  helped pay for him to be able to bring  his equipment back from New York so we  can start up shop all over again  and it was only because he treated his  employees so well prior that he was able  to call on them to be able to help him  out when he really needed help he  believed in that philosophy even when he  got richer and was doing a lot better  with this company the classic example is  in 1929 when everything crashed started  the Great Depression he was in the  process of building new constructions  for his little town and somebody came to  him with an invention it was a steam  shovel they said this steam shovel can  help you save a lot of costs it can cut  the work of 40 employees and have one  person do the job of 40 and he said look  at what's going on in the economy these  days get rid of the shovel hire the 40  workers and he was able to build up a  lot of community support because of his  philosophy of being able to continue to  give back help others and be respectful  so think about your own business  think about the people you've seen your  daily lives your employees your  partner's your investors your customers  the media anybody would come across your  next-door neighbor try to treat them  with respect because you never know when  you're going to need to call on their  help someday for your business I hope  you've enjoyed this edition of modeling  the masters I wanted to remind you that  Milton Hershey started the business was  an 18 year old kid didn't know anything  had no money the hundred dollar loan  from his aunt to get the business  started and he was able to build it up  where now it's a five billion dollar  company with 11,000 employees you can  achieve the same results with your  business if you really want to follow  the lessons from Milton Hershey if you  are persistent if you innovate any treat  people with respect you too can build a  great company I hope you've enjoyed this  edition if you want to learn more about  famous entrepreneurs you can check out  our website at Evan Carmichael com  and I've recently launched a new blog as  well the link is listed below that just  talks about the famous entrepreneurs and  how to model the success of famous  entrepreneurs I also wanted to thank our  sponsors  fanta media for all the great video work  that they've done on these episodes  and I look forward to seeing you at the  next edition of modeling the Masters  you
 

